  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The relations&nbsp;of Young&#39;s modulus,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi></math>, bulk modulus,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi></math>, the modulus of rigidity,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#951;</mi></math>&nbsp;and Poisson&#39;s ratio,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#963;</mi></math>&nbsp;are given as</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>K</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#963;</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#951;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#963;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>From equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math>, we have</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#951;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#963;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>K</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#963;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#963;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>K</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#951;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#951;</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math></p>",
